  "name": "Sixteenth Stutter Response",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A ratchet bar of sixteenth-note stabs that answers the triplet call: bright metallic hits with a rest at the end of each beat, over a clean sine sub that gates with them. Play: hold F1, G1 or A#1 at 140-150 BPM for a full bar of stutter, or drop it as a fill; the pattern restarts on every new note. Macros: Stutter Depth takes the bar from a steady tone to hard gated stabs, Metal adds bite and FM edge, Rest Length smears the gaps between hits and Shimmer adds a sixteenth-note flutter on top.",
